ction in `calc.py` was returning the difference of two numbers instead of their sum, causing the test `test_add(2, 3)` to return `-1` instead of `5`.\n\n## Root Cause\nLine 2 in `calc.py` used the subtraction operator (`-`) instead of the addition operator (`+`):\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a - b  # Wrong\n```\n\n## Fix\nChanged the operator from subtraction to addition:\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b  # Correct\n```\n\n## Testing\nThe fix resolves the failing `test_add` test case, which now correctly expects `add(2, 3)` to equal `5`.\n"}}, "apiBlockIndex": 1, "requestId": "req_011Cfu1bCkxQjJWLNXs3MtxZ", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "c8456d6f-9aef-4e02-be21-e7cc73e94e8c", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T18:14:06.151Z", "perTurnEffort": null, "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "claude-desktop", "cwd": "C:\\work\\repo", "sessionId": "c7f77658-bc52-48dd-b965-eb3548ca5432", "version": "2.1.287", "gitBranch": "master"}
